WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.986
Do not build on banned sand.

00:00:01.986 --> 00:00:06.950
A clever idea that violates the law or a platform ToS is a future wipeout.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.267
This lesson is about illegal/tos death checks.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.921
Don't build on banned sand.

00:00:10.921 --> 00:00:13.238
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:16.547
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:21.512
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.512 --> 00:00:25.152
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:25.472 --> 00:00:32.108
Run a death check: illegal activity, regulated claims you cannot support, and platform rules that ban your distribution.

00:00:32.108 --> 00:00:35.057
Remember the objective: run a ToS risk check.

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:39.113
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:43.537
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.537 --> 00:00:47.592
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.592 --> 00:00:52.016
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.336 --> 00:00:54.348
Write the risk in one line.

00:00:54.348 --> 00:00:58.708
If the path depends on a ToS gray zone, pick a cleaner lane.

